#: ../../source/depd_Readme.md:10
msgid "Deprecate all the things"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/depd_Readme.md:12
msgid "With great modules comes great responsibility; mark things deprecated!"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/depd_Readme.md:14
msgid "Install"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/depd_Readme.md:16
msgid "This module is installed directly using `npm`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/depd_Readme.md:22
msgid ""
"This module can also be bundled with systems like "
"[Browserify](http://browserify.org/) or "
"[webpack](https://webpack.github.io/), though by default this module will"
" alter it's API to no longer display or track deprecations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/depd_Readme.md:27
msgid "API"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/depd_Readme.md:35
msgid ""
"This library allows you to display deprecation messages to your users. "
"This library goes above and beyond with deprecation warnings by "
"introspection of the call stack (but only the bits that it is interested "
"in)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/depd_Readme.md:40
msgid ""
"Instead of just warning on the first invocation of a deprecated function "
"and never again, this module will warn on the first invocation of a "
"deprecated function per unique call site, making it ideal to alert users "
"of all deprecated uses across the code base, rather than just whatever "
"happens to execute first."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/depd_Readme.md:46
msgid ""
"The deprecation warnings from this module also include the file and line "
"information for the call into the module that the deprecated function was"
" in."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/depd_Readme.md:50
msgid ""
"**NOTE** this library has a similar interface to the `debug` module, and "
"this module uses the calling file to get the boundary for the call "
"stacks, so you should always create a new `deprecate` object in each file"
" and not within some central file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/depd_Readme.md:55
msgid "depd(namespace)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/depd_Readme.md:57
msgid ""
"Create a new deprecate function that uses the given namespace name in the"
" messages and will display the call site prior to the stack entering the "
"file this function was called from. It is highly suggested you use the "
"name of your module as the namespace."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/depd_Readme.md:62
msgid "deprecate(message)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/depd_Readme.md:64
msgid ""
"Call this function from deprecated code to display a deprecation message."
" This message will appear once per unique caller site. Caller site is the"
" first call site in the stack in a different file from the caller of this"
" function."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/depd_Readme.md:69
msgid ""
"If the message is omitted, a message is generated for you based on the "
"site of the `deprecate()` call and will display the name of the function "
"called, similar to the name displayed in a stack trace."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/depd_Readme.md:73
msgid "deprecate.function(fn, message)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/depd_Readme.md:75
msgid ""
"Call this function to wrap a given function in a deprecation message on "
"any call to the function. An optional message can be supplied to provide "
"a custom message."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/depd_Readme.md:79
msgid "deprecate.property(obj, prop, message)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/depd_Readme.md:81
msgid ""
"Call this function to wrap a given property on object in a deprecation "
"message on any accessing or setting of the property. An optional message "
"can be supplied to provide a custom message."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/depd_Readme.md:85
msgid ""
"The method must be called on the object where the property belongs (not "
"inherited from the prototype)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/depd_Readme.md:88
msgid ""
"If the property is a data descriptor, it will be converted to an accessor"
" descriptor in order to display the deprecation message."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/depd_Readme.md:91
msgid "process.on('deprecation', fn)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/depd_Readme.md:93
msgid ""
"This module will allow easy capturing of deprecation errors by emitting "
"the errors as the type \"deprecation\" on the global `process`. If there "
"are no listeners for this type, the errors are written to STDERR as "
"normal, but if there are any listeners, nothing will be written to STDERR"
" and instead only emitted. From there, you can write the errors in a "
"different format or to a logging source."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/depd_Readme.md:100
msgid ""
"The error represents the deprecation and is emitted only once with the "
"same rules as writing to STDERR. The error has the following properties:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/depd_Readme.md:103
msgid "`message` - This is the message given by the library"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/depd_Readme.md:104
msgid "`name` - This is always `'DeprecationError'`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/depd_Readme.md:105
msgid "`namespace` - This is the namespace the deprecation came from"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/depd_Readme.md:106
msgid "`stack` - This is the stack of the call to the deprecated thing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/depd_Readme.md:108
msgid "Example `error.stack` output:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/depd_Readme.md:119
msgid "process.env.NO_DEPRECATION"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/depd_Readme.md:121
msgid ""
"As a user of modules that are deprecated, the environment variable "
"`NO_DEPRECATION` is provided as a quick solution to silencing deprecation"
" warnings from being output. The format of this is similar to that of "
"`DEBUG`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/depd_Readme.md:129
msgid ""
"This will suppress deprecations from being output for \"my-module\" and "
"\"othermod\". The value is a list of comma-separated namespaces. To "
"suppress every warning across all namespaces, use the value `*` for a "
"namespace."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/depd_Readme.md:133
msgid ""
"Providing the argument `--no-deprecation` to the `node` executable will "
"suppress all deprecations (only available in Node.js 0.8 or higher)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/depd_Readme.md:136
msgid ""
"**NOTE** This will not suppress the deperecations given to any "
"\"deprecation\" event listeners, just the output to STDERR."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/depd_Readme.md:139
msgid "process.env.TRACE_DEPRECATION"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/depd_Readme.md:141
msgid ""
"As a user of modules that are deprecated, the environment variable "
"`TRACE_DEPRECATION` is provided as a solution to getting more detailed "
"location information in deprecation warnings by including the entire "
"stack trace. The format of this is the same as `NO_DEPRECATION`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/depd_Readme.md:150
msgid ""
"This will include stack traces for deprecations being output for \"my-"
"module\" and \"othermod\". The value is a list of comma-separated "
"namespaces. To trace every warning across all namespaces, use the value "
"`*` for a namespace."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/depd_Readme.md:154
msgid ""
"Providing the argument `--trace-deprecation` to the `node` executable "
"will trace all deprecations (only available in Node.js 0.8 or higher)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/depd_Readme.md:157
msgid ""
"**NOTE** This will not trace the deperecations silenced by "
"`NO_DEPRECATION`."
msgstr ""

